!!<*yamlover: $defs: chapter>
Conformance
description: the yaml-test-suite stance — accept everything except the documented divergences
- >
  Because yamlover is a close-but-distinct language, the YAML conformance corpus (yaml-test-suite) is
  run as "accept all positive cases except a documented divergence allowlist" — the anchor/alias cases
  are diverges-by-design, not failures. The walk parses `.yaml`/`.yml` files with YAML link semantics,
  concrete-aware as everywhere.
- >
  For a side-by-side feel of the divergence, the repository keeps a worked pair:
  `examples/05-tour.yaml` is plain YAML — native anchor sharing, no paths — and `examples/06-tour.yo`
  is the same data with the full pointer layer.
